{"description":"Have you heard the term “GMO” and never given it a second thought? Or have you wondered why there is so much debate about genetically modified organisms?\nWell, you’re in luck.\nJoin Quantum Leaps youth leaders Yasmeen Lopez and Isabella Ciaccia with researchers and experts as they unpack the science behind genetic modification and answer your biggest questions about food, farming, ethics, and innovation!\nNo background in science is needed, as this event is free and open to everyone, regardless of age or experience with the topic.\nEvent Details:\n📅 Date: Thursday, October 8th, 2026\n🕕 Time: 6:15-7:30 pm\n📍 Location: Bloor/Gladstone Library, 1101 Bloor St W, Toronto\n🎟️ Admission: FREE for all ages\n🍽️ Snacks and refreshments will be provided!\n\nFeatured Panelists:\n⭐ Dr. Alexander Hall, Assistant Professor in Science Communication at McMaster University\n⭐ Dr. Carlos Alberto Arnillas, Research Associate, Ecological Modelling Laboratory at the University of Toronto\n⭐ Poornima Goudar, Masters of Public Health (Epidemiology) student at the University of Toronto\n\nKnow a friend or family member that is interested in GMOs? Share this event with them! \n\nThis is not an event hosted or sponsored by the Toronto Public Library.","organizer":"Isabella Ciaccia"}